z9x-0011: audio resends awaited until the packet's deadline, all gaps asked for, counts

Ours (Z9xAirPlay), against FDH2/UxPlay master 3dbf7ce after z9x-0001..0010 (paths relative
to UxPlay/lib). Applied by jni/build_native.sh inside a copy of UxPlay/lib with
patch -p1 --fuzz=0.
- raop.h: two optional callbacks at the end of raop_callbacks_t. audio_resend_deadline
  gives the CLOCK_MONOTONIC time by which an audio packet must reach the player (its play
  time less the output latency and a margin), audio_resend_stats receives resend counts.
- raop_buffer.c: z9x-0010 gave up a gap once the first packet after it had waited a fixed
  100 ms: far too early for ALAC (about 1.7 s left to play it), sometimes too late for
  mirroring AAC-ELD. The gap is now given up at the missing packet's deadline (its RTP
  timestamp interpolated between the last packet played and the first one after the gap);
  the fixed 100 ms remains only when the player gives no deadline. Every gap in the buffer is
  asked for as soon as it is seen (upstream: only the first gap, asked again on every
  received packet), a gap still missing again every 50 ms, at most 8 gaps per pass. Counts:
  packets requested (once each), resends received in time, resends received after their gap
  was given up, packets given up.
- raop_rtp.c: the dequeue / resend / statistics step is one function, also run after a
  resent packet (played at once instead of with the next data packet) and on the 5 ms select
  timeout (a gap is given up at its deadline even while no packet arrives).
